 </div> </div>I mean, that goes without saying. And I don't want to imagine it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T13:15:46-07:00","id":1377564,"title":"","content":"As a Makara I would definitely go on awesome underwater trip around the world, seeing the wonders of underwater life firsthand, without that annoying pressure/air troubles. <br /> Keeping a chamber/exit at the bottom of the ocean, possibly with live-in monsters could also be very useful.<br /> <br /> Would travel to Mars through astral and set up a chamber there too! Maybe also on other planets... but they are even more inhospitable. Welcome to space. <br /> <br /> work as a stage magician with that merit that allows to pull things straight from the lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:34:33-07:00","id":1382856,"title":"","content":"The first time I read the main Beast book, I found myself thinking how easy it would be to be a Private Investigator and use that to hide your feeding in plain sight.<br /> <br /> As a Eshmaki, From the Shadows, would make following non-supernaturals super easy, and then a tiny camera or recording device to discover all their secrets.<br /> <br /> Mimir's Wisdom and Eye of Heaven to make your job even easier.<br /> <br /> For a Sam Spade type, you could use True Friend and Retainer to make the traditional harried underpaid but dedicated receptionist/secretary. You could also attach a one of the part of their lair to their actual office and include lair traits like dim lighting and rough terrain (cluttered office), to give it the right feel.<br /> <br /> For a Mike Hammer Type an Anakim is the obvious choice.<br /> <br /> I thought it would be hilarious to do Magnum PI as a Makara. All the accoutrements could be done through merits. Magnum's Guest House could easily hide the entrance to his lair and include defenses like being disgusting and have a terrible smell. Higgins is a great example of a Retainer, run really well by the GM. The moustache, must have magical powers. May be it stretches into a animated ropes instead of the traditional tentacles?<br /> <br /> Please be kind, this is my first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26098-framboisedelanut","name":"Framboisedelanut","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T18:12:39-07:00","id":1382863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Framboisedelanut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1135731-fun-activities-as-a-beast?p=1382856#post1382856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first time I read the main Beast book, I found myself thinking how easy it would be to be a Private Investigator and use that to hide your feeding in plain sight.<br /> <br /> As a Eshmaki, From the Shadows, would make following non-supernaturals super easy, and then a tiny camera or recording device to discover all their secrets.<br /> <br /> Mimir's Wisdom and Eye of Heaven to make your job even easier.<br /> <br /> For a Sam Spade type, you could use True Friend and Retainer to make the traditional harried underpaid but dedicated receptionist/secretary. You could also attach a one of the part of their lair to their actual office and include lair traits like dim lighting and rough terrain (cluttered office), to give it the right feel.<br /> <br /> For a Mike Hammer Type an Anakim is the obvious choice.<br /> <br /> I thought it would be hilarious to do Magnum PI as a Makara. All the accoutrements could be done through merits. Magnum's Guest House could easily hide the entrance to his lair and include defenses like being disgusting and have a terrible smell. Higgins is a great example of a Retainer, run really well by the GM. The moustache, must have magical powers. May be it stretches into a animated ropes instead of the traditional tentacles?<br /> <br /> Please be kind, this is my first post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well your first post is really well done. Its exactly the kind of stuff we want on this particular thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-22T02:18:50-07:00","id":1383110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Framboisedelanut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1135731-fun-activities-as-a-beast?p=1382856#post1382856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first time I read the main Beast book, I found myself thinking how easy it would be to be a Private Investigator and use that to hide your feeding in plain sight.<br /> <br /> As a Eshmaki, From the Shadows, would make following non-supernaturals super easy, and then a tiny camera or recording device to discover all their secrets.<br /> <br /> Mimir's Wisdom and Eye of Heaven to make your job even easier.<br /> <br /> For a Sam Spade type, you could use True Friend and Retainer to make the traditional harried underpaid but dedicated receptionist/secretary. You could also attach a one of the part of their lair to their actual office and include lair traits like dim lighting and rough terrain (cluttered office), to give it the right feel.<br /> <br /> For a Mike Hammer Type an Anakim is the obvious choice.<br /> <br /> I thought it would be hilarious to do Magnum PI as a Makara. All the accoutrements could be done through merits. Magnum's Guest House could easily hide the entrance to his lair and include defenses like being disgusting and have a terrible smell. Higgins is a great example of a Retainer, run really well by the GM. The moustache, must have magical powers. May be it stretches into a animated ropes instead of the traditional tentacles?<br /> <br /> Please be kind, this is my first post.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It would certainly be a lot of fun to be a trained detective who ended up being a Beast (as long as Hunger and job fit together somewhat), because now you can not only do your job more easily, but you can Jason Bourne (place alternative archetype detective here) the shit out of it.<br /> <br /> Same applies to other jobs that fit well: A boxer (e.g. with Unbreakable, Looming Presence, Relentless Hunter and Monster From The Deep) could be near-unbeatable in the ring (especially at low Satiety). <br /> <br /> <br /> Another fun activity: step up your cosplay (or Larp) a bit by including fitting Atavisms - a Hulk cosplay with Cyclopean Strength, a Wings of the Raptor-aided Spiderman, Storm-Lashed to add some gusts of wind to your 'magic'...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}